# Hand history fixtures are byte-exact evidence, not source code.
#
# Real exports ship with CRLF, bare CR, UTF-16LE and cp1252 bytes, and the
# parsers exist precisely to survive that. Git's autocrlf normalisation
# (core.autocrlf=input is set on at least one machine here) rewrites CRLF to
# LF on commit, which silently turns a CRLF test case into an LF one while the
# working tree still looks correct. Mark them binary so the stored blob is the
# original bytes.
fixtures/** -text -diff
gg-hh/** -text -diff
weplay-hh/** -text -diff
backend/test/fixtures/** -text -diff
